==English==
{{wikipedia}}
[[Image:Australia-wombat.jpg|thumb]]

===Etymology===
{{bor+|en|xdk|wambad}}, {{m|xdk|wambaj}}, or {{m|xdk|wambag}}. It was originally written {{m|en|whom-batt}} in English.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈwɑmˌbæt/|a=US}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈwɒm.bæt/|a=UK,CA}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-wombat.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɑmbæt|ɒmbæt|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Any of several [[herbivorous]], burrowing [[marsupial]]s, of the family {{taxfmt|Vombatidae|family}}, mainly found in southern and eastern [[Australia]].
# {{lb|en|AU|slang}} A [[slow]] and [[stupid]] person; a [[dullard]].

